{
  "findings": [
    "The cyclic/ballot route does not currently prove the claim. For an even suffix R=2J, write a=1-{beta tau}, H_j=sum_{i<=j}B_i, and d=K-2 beta J. Centering by the actual endpoint gives u_j=H_j-jK/J and the exact identity log_2 z_j=a+u_j+(j d/J). Thus the low/non-low test is a first-passage test for a rational-lattice bridge against the tilted affine barrier log_2(eta)-a-jd/J, not against a fixed zero barrier.",
    "A pair-total cyclic shift preserves the even-suffix weight: under the uniform raw weak-composition law, P((B_1,...,B_J)=b | sum B_i=K) is proportional to product_i(b_i+1). Hence exchangeability and rotation invariance are available in the even case. They do not by themselves give an occupation count, because the barrier contains the phase a and the slope jd/J. Since d is only bounded, the cumulative tilt is O(1), comparable with the barrier, and cannot be discarded. Centered ties also occur on the 1/J lattice; strict versus non-strict crossings and zero/near-zero visits require an explicit uniform estimate.",
    "Raw-coordinate cyclic arguments do not automatically repair even-time sampling. Pairing changes the increment law to the weighted law above, while an odd suffix has a distinguished singleton: conditional on its value s, the pair total is K-s, and one must sum uniformly over s with the corresponding weight. No displayed reduction supplies a parity-preserving cyclic lemma with these affine and boundary conventions.",
    "The beta-binomial marginal formula, even if used, controls one time only and cannot imply the needed exponential lower-tail bound for occupation. The exact resonance coefficient formula likewise is only a finite counting identity and supplies no bound excluding resonant useful blocks."
  ],
  "claim_status": "OPEN: neither a rigorous proof nor an actual accessible counterexample has been established.",
  "first_missing_step": {
    "lemma": "Before adding bounded-positive and nonresonance marks, prove the following strictly narrower, parity-correct bridge estimate. For fixed eta>0 and lambda>0, uniformly over all sufficiently large actual R=2J+epsilon, epsilon in {0,1}, all admissible K,tau, and the induced weak-composition law (including the singleton summation when epsilon=1), with a=1-{beta tau}, establish E[exp(-lambda M_{J,epsilon}) | S_R=K and the stipulated exact data] <= C/J, where M_{J,epsilon}=#{1<=j<=J: a+H_j-2 beta j >= log_2 eta}.",
    "why_first": "This is the unmarked occupation estimate needed before one can control the number of blocks that are simultaneously non-low, bounded-positive, and nonresonant. It is strictly narrower than the target because it ignores block grouping, the positive alphabet restriction, and resonance deletion.",
    "what_is_missing": "A proof must explicitly handle the rational ties in u_j, the bounded affine phase and endpoint tilt, the even-time sampling, and the odd singleton. No supplied identity establishes this uniform Laplace inequality."
  },
  "unexpected_findings": [
    "The cyclic symmetry that survives is weighted pair-block symmetry, not uniform composition symmetry of the centered pair increments; treating the latter as an ordinary zero-drift ballot bridge would be an additional unproved step."
  ]
}
